<title>UK: Le Shuttle resume's traffic.</title>
<headline>Le Shuttle resume's traffic.</headline>
<dateline>CHERITON, England 1996-12-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Eurotunnel Plc SA's Le Shuttle passenger car service resumed on Tuesday morning as planned, three weeks after a fire partially closed down the fixed link, according to a Reuters reporter travelling with the the first train to go through the tunnel.</p>
<p>The first train, carrying 61 vehicles, left Coquelles terminal, near Calais, at 0630 GMT and arrived at the Cheriton terminal 50 minutes later, the reporter said.</p>
<p>The trip through the tunnel was about five to 15 minutes longer than a normal crossing due to damage from the November 18 fire.</p>
</text>
